# The whole build runs on Linux, so text that is consumed by bash, patch(1)
# or git apply must be LF on disk. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true commits CRLF and every patch hunk fails to apply on the
# runner with "Hunk #1 FAILED" -- which looks like a source mismatch.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.patch     text eol=lf
*.env       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.config    text eol=lf
